  // R57.M4-003 (paideia-os #1799): sys_taskinfo -- one-shot marker emitted
  // by the M0 witness that first walks the task pool through the new
  // syscall path.  Declaration lives here per the em-dash-dropped
  // convention (memo §5.1 option B): the fingerprint body carries the
  // classic UPPERCASE tag inside a `[legacy: ...]` bracket so operator
  // grep parity with the pre-R51 wire is preserved, while the primary
  // body is a lowercase English narrative that verify-fingerprint-
  // coverage.sh's OK_TOK regex recognises via the `ok` token.
  //
  // Byte count NUL-inclusive per #699 discipline:
  //   "sys taskinfo ok [legacy: SYS TASKINFO OK]" = 41 chars + NUL = 42
  //
  // No emit site is added by this file -- a witness that exercises the
  // syscall end-to-end (kernel-side call through dispatch_taskinfo,
  // observing the record on wire) is the natural first consumer; that
  // witness is out of scope for the M0 body-plus-shim landing and
  // arrives with the M1 comm[16] wiring per src/kernel/core/sched/
  // task_info.pdx §Name field.  Declaring the tag now rather than
  // co-landing with the witness keeps the fingerprint namespace stable
  // across the M0 -> M1 transition and lets the M1 witness commit
  // stand alone against a golden without also touching keys.pdx.
  pub let tag_sys_taskinfo_ok : [u8; 42] = "sys taskinfo ok [legacy: SYS TASKINFO OK]\0"

  // R57.M4-004 (paideia-os #1800): sys_mountinfo -- one-shot marker
  // for the M0 witness that first walks the mount table through the
  // new syscall path.  Declaration lives here per the em-dash-dropped
  // convention (memo §5.1 option B): the fingerprint body carries the
  // classic UPPERCASE tag inside a `[legacy: ...]` bracket so
  // operator grep parity with the pre-R51 wire is preserved, while
  // the primary body is a lowercase English narrative that verify-
  // fingerprint-coverage.sh's OK_TOK regex recognises via the `ok`
  // token.
  //
  // Byte count NUL-inclusive per #699 discipline:
  //   "sys mountinfo ok [legacy: SYS MOUNTINFO OK]" = 43 chars + NUL = 44
  //
  // No emit site is added by this file -- an iterator syscall called
  // up to MOUNT_MAX (8) times per /bin/mount invocation would inflate
  // the ring with duplicate `sys mountinfo ok` lines for no
  // diagnostic gain.  Same declared-but-unemitted pattern as
  // tag_sys_taskinfo_ok above.  A future one-shot witness that
  // exercises the syscall end-to-end (kernel-side call through
  // dispatch_mountinfo, observing the record on wire) is the natural
  // first consumer and emits the tag exactly once at witness top.
  // Declaring the tag now rather than co-landing with the witness
  // keeps the fingerprint namespace stable across the M0 -> M1
  // transition and lets the witness commit stand alone against a
  // golden without also touching keys.pdx.
  pub let tag_sys_mountinfo_ok : [u8; 44] = "sys mountinfo ok [legacy: SYS MOUNTINFO OK]\0"

