  // R100-PREP-002 (#2008): connected-UDP boot witness fingerprint. The
  // boot_r100_udp_socket witness (src/kernel/boot/witness/r100_udp_
  // socket.pdx) mints two KIND_UDP_SOCKET caps, binds+connects both,
  // sends one 5-byte datagram from A to B over the loopback fast path,
  // and asserts recv returns exactly 5 bytes byte-for-byte identical
  // to the sent payload. Success emits the fingerprint below via
  // klog_s1_d2 with two decimal KVs (port_a, port_b), same wrapper +
  // shape r89_tui_canvas / r100_tls_trust use for their own two-KV
  // emits. Deliberately all-lowercase with no bracketed "[legacy: ...
  // OK]" suffix, matching the r89/r100 brand-new-narrative-tag
  // posture: no standalone uppercase "OK" token means
  // tools/verify-fingerprint-coverage.sh's OK_TOK extractor does not
  // require golden coverage or an allowlist entry for the outer line
  // (only the inner mint/read markers below need entries -- but there
  // is only one, "boot udp sock ok", and we do not carry any inner
  // "OK" tag from net/udp_socket.pdx since the UDP substrate emits no
  // klog lines of its own for send/recv on the hot path).
